  "notes": "{締|し}め{括|くく}る means to bring something to a fitting conclusion or wrap-up. It implies a deliberate, satisfying ending rather than simply stopping.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pattern: [event/speech]を{締|し}め{括|くく}る\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- スピーチを{締|し}め{括|くく}る: to conclude a speech\n- {一年|いちねん}を{締|し}め{括|くく}る: to close out the year\n- 〜で{締|し}め{括|くく}る: to wrap up with ~\n- {最後|さいご}を{締|し}め{括|くく}る: to bring the end together\n\nRELATED NOUN:\n- {締|し}め{括|くく}り: conclusion, wrap-up\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {終|お}える: to finish (neutral, general)\n- まとめる: to summarize, to put together\n- {結|むす}ぶ: to conclude (more formal, used for contracts and agreements)",
